{%- doc -%}
  ArchiveOS — catalogue feed.

  A JSON array of every playable artifact, rendered once per page
  alongside the transport deck.

  WHY THIS EXISTS

  The deck's queue is normally the cards on the current page, in DOM
  order. That is the right default — it matches what the visitor can
  see, and it respects facet filtering for free, because Horizon's
  facets re-render the grid server-side rather than hiding cards.

  But some templates render no cards at all. The product page is the
  clearest case: it has product-recommendations, which renders
  through the resource-card chain and emits no .archive-card. On
  those pages the queue was empty, so pressing next — or reaching the
  end of a track — did nothing at all.

  This feed is the fallback. archive-card-ui.js prefers visible
  cards and drops to this only when there are none.

  WHY NOT A FETCH

  Metafields are not exposed by /products.json, and the audio URL
  lives in custom.audio_preview (a file_reference). Only Liquid can
  resolve it. A fetch would need a dedicated section endpoint and a
  round trip; embedding costs roughly 3 KB gzipped and cannot fail
  at runtime.

  COST

  Rendered on every page, including pages that will never use it.
  Capped at 50 artifacts — Liquid's default for an unpaginated
  collection loop. If the catalogue outgrows that, this should
  become a paginated section endpoint rather than a larger blob.

  The record shape is defined once in archive-track-record.liquid.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- capture archive_feed_records -%}
  {%- for product in collections.all.products limit: 50 -%}
    {%- capture record -%}
      {%- render 'archive-track-record', product: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- assign record = record | strip -%}

    {%- if record != blank -%}
      {%- if archive_feed_emitted == 'yes' -%},{%- endif -%}
      {{- record -}}
      {%- assign archive_feed_emitted = 'yes' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- assign archive_feed_records = archive_feed_records | strip -%}

{%- if archive_feed_records != blank -%}
  <script type="application/json" data-archive-feed>
    [{{ archive_feed_records }}]
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
